 Excellent question.

 Answer:

 > "Because the problem wasn't simply a stuck Nexus service. The restart helped us rule out a transient service-level issue, but the underlying problem was related to storage consumption and later a corrupted proxy repository. Restarting a service can't resolve a storage snapshot retaining deleted data or corrupted repository content."

 This demonstrates good troubleshooting maturity.

