 # If they ask "How did you know the storage issue was related to the slowness?"

 Say:

 > "We correlated the timing of the performance degradation with the storage condition observed in the Nexus logs. After removing unnecessary data and increasing storage capacity, the NPM builds improved from highly inconsistent behavior to approximately two-minute completion. That gave us evidence that storage pressure was contributing to the performance problem."

 Notice the wording: **"contributing to"**, rather than claiming storage was the only cause when the RCA itself says the high-volume traffic investigation was still in progress.

 That's technically safer.

